I just noticed pkgload has a new argument, `debug`, which prevents `devtools::load_all()` from inserting the -O0 debugger flag, the culprit of the Windows file too big error. Try `devtools::load_all(debug = FALSE)`

On Thu, Jun 11, 2026 at 12:54 PM 'Kelli Johnson - NOAA Federal' via TMB Users <tmb-...@googlegroups.com> wrote:

> In a recent conversation with Ian Taylor, this problem has surfaced again but Ian knew how to handle it because of knowledge provided by Andrea through FIMS development. I am wondering how we fix the issue permanently rather than requiring the Windows work around? For example, can we add something to the Makevars.win file? I was not able to successfully do anything to it though myself to get devtools::load_all() to still work. I was able to add a .Renviron file to the FIMS directory with `PKG_BUILD_EXTRA_FLAGS=false` and then devtools::load_all() worked for me without the `withr::local_options()` call. I know essentially they are doing the same thing but it is a pain to need to remember the withr call and new developers often do not know how to fix the problem. So, can we just add this .Renviron file to our package and encourage others to do so as well?
>
